    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="a16c95c2-8a00-5bf5-8def-e5b6e8111881" activityNameId="c8da4a86-c0f5-5e04-a7ab-3f4802cf7a71" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, sewer system, vitrified clay pipe, DN 800, profile 3</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, sewer system, vitrified clay pipe, DN 800, profile 3
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 16171406-e9f5-4df8-8da3-6d1ae223c4e8
This process models deconstruction and end-of-life treatment for 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with vitrified clay pipe. DN 800, profile 3 according to SIA 190. Trench depth: 3 meters. This process includes the deconstruction phase (C1), transport phase (C2), treatment/ recycling phase (C3), and final disposal phase (C4) for 1 meter of sewer system with vitrified clay pipe, DN 800, profile 3. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 800, profile 3 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Vitrified clay pipe, ID 792 mm, outer diameter 932 mm, wall thickness 70 mm, 379 kg/m, 2000 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_16171406-e9f5-4df8-8da3-6d1ae223c4e8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
